@document.meta
title: Modals
description: jagaranth lexicon article
categories: [ conlang, lexicon, grammar, article, jagaranth ]
@end


* MODALS


|------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------|
| :: kush :: = wanna (Desire)                                | :: gig :: = to not want (Negative Desire)                      |
| :: flar :: = tryna (Attempt)                               | :: flaribor :: trying not to (Attempt at Achieving a Negative) |
| :: jip :: = finna (Immediate Intent)                       | :: jipibor :: about to take steps so smthg wont happen         |
| :: ben :: will :: (Future Certainty)                       | :: benbor :: won't (future certainty of a negative)            |
| :: tên :: = can (Physical Ability)                         | :: tênbor :: = can't (Negative Physical Ability)               |
| :: lich :: = may (Permission)                              | :: finbor :: may not (Prohibition) (a double negative)         |
| :: kor :: = must (Strict Obligation)                       | :: reb :: must not (Strict Negative Obligation)                |
| :: dix :: = should (Recommendation/Advice)                 | :: dixibor :: should not (Informal Negative Obligation)        |
| :: tezh :: = might (Possibility)                           | :: tezhbor :: might not (Negative Possibility)                 |
| :: shen :: = must be (logical Certainty based on evidence) | :: shenbor :: must not be (based on reason and evidence)       |
|------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------|

** USAGE and EXAMPLES
   - example:
        - tethot panâlem-sis, tezh âr-bârkexâlem {^ footnote}[see footnote]
            - parse :: 3rdSgSentiantPronoun.Accusative see.Finite.1stSgSentientSubject, MightModal ToCompletion-gun.Applicative.Finite.!stSgSentientSubject
            - translation :: If I see him, I might shoot him dead.

^ footnote 
the object *tethot* need not be expressed in the followup clause bc occurring first it is emphasized and remains in mind

- example:
    - ___kush gaktâlem tetheg___
    - I wanna dance with you.

- example:
    - ***gig jûkâlem jizixoteps ::*** I dont want your meth.

- example:
    - ***jûjor kush jûkâleps jizixot meth foifirot ??***
    - You wanna do meth or cocaine?

- example
    - ***lîz tezh jûkâlem foifirûrotech ??***
    - parse of foifirûrotech :: cocaine.Genitive.Accusative.Unowned
    - Where might I partake of illicit cocaine?

- example:
    - ***benbor korodâleps ::***
        - Thou shalt not kill.

- example:
    - jûjor Marish am tokom kensosûr spelâleps wel ??
        - Is Venus the far destination of which you speak?

+ example:
    + reb thiktâleps-mot
    + You may not touch me.

+ example:
    + jip âr-bârkexâlem vêgorotech ::
        + I'm finna to shoot the wild wolf to death.

+ example:
    + dixibor kafâleps korodârên
